  "eigen_power: opposite-sign tie on the wide path: lambda is 3.3.3's bits");
assert_eq(load64(g2a_evec + 8), 0xBFEFFFFFFFFFF000,
  "eigen_power: opposite-sign tie on the wide path: v1 is 3.3.3's bits");
# (9) THE WIDE RUN TESTS ITS VECTOR, NOT ONLY ITS ESTIMATE. [[a00, -3.92e285, 5.64, 0],
# [0, -9.03e-128, -5.69e284, 0], [0, 0, a22, 0], [8.69, -9.43e-297, -0.796, a33]],
# a00 = 2.66e-89, a22 = 9.75, a33 = -6.39 (|lambda_2/lambda_1| = 0.655): the dominant
# eigenvector of a22, scaled, is (1, -2.5e-285, 4.3e-569, v3), its third component below
# the f64 range. 3.3.3: Ok(0) and a33. The wide run's estimate is a22 before its v3 has
# settled, so without its vector test it returns an unconverged eigenvector. Exact v3:
# a30 / (a22 - a33) plus terms far below an ulp, rounded 0x3FE13A453E9B4CB1 (Fractions);
# now 2.7e-13 from it, inside tol / (1 - 0.655).
# [measured: eigen_power fixture probe and wide-run vector-test mutant, base and 3.3.4 trees, cycc 6.6.14, 2026-10-03]
var _k4e9 = ganita_mat_new(4, 4);
